* The digits of a whole number, last first, and their sum.
* ip(n/10) is n without its last digit.
1.1 Set d = n - 10·ip(n/10).
1.2 Type d in form 1.
1.3 Set s = s+d.
1.4 Set n = ip(n/10).
1.5 To step 1.1 if n > 0.
1.6 Type s in form 2.
Form 1:
digit _
Form 2:
sum  __

Set n = 271828.
Set s = 0.
Do part 1.

* dp and xp take a number apart the other way: digit part and exponent part.
Set x = 271828.
Type dp(x), xp(x), dp(x)·10*xp(x).
